{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_435","type":"reasoning","text":"The `artifacts/policy-doc-truthfulness/report.json` is regenerated but gitignored, so it's not part of the change set. Good.\n\nNow let's finalize. Let me also double-check the README review conclusion — the AGENTS.md says doc sync rule applies for functional/architecture changes. E02 is internal evaluation only; no user-visible change. Reasonable.\n\nLet me do a final read of the two harness specs and the rule spec to make sure there are no machine-specific paths that would fail validateSpecPortability (already validated: validate --no-diff passed, which includes portability). Good.\n\nOne more consideration: `check-spec-lifecycle.mjs` exit 1. This is a pre-existing failure on 2 other specs. My spec has lifecycleStatus. I should note this honestly. Actually — I could improve the repo by adding lifecycleStatus to those two pre-existing specs, but they're outside targetScope and the task says do exactly what's asked with surgical precision and don't fix unrelated bugs. I'll leave them and mention it.\n\nLet me now also verify that the E02 fixture's `preregistration.notes` claims match. Fine.\n\nLet me quickly review the two test files once more for any leftover issues (e.g. the `comparePairedBinary` unused import? no). Also check that `PairedAblationBudgetCheck` etc. imports are all used to avoid noUnusedLocals errors — but tsconfig.test.json sets noUnusedLocals: false, and tests use tsconfig.test.json. Good. But the eslint config might flag unused vars. In agent-dev-paired-ablation.test.ts I import `PAIRED_ABLATION_CONDITIONS` (used), `PAIRED_ABLATION_GATE_STATUSES` (used), `PAIRED_ABLATION_VERSION` (used), `analyzePairedAblation`(used), `buildTrialPlan`(used), `buildTrialRecord`(used), `cohensH`(used), `comparePairedBinary`(used), `deriveTrialSeed`(used), `expandCaseFacts`(used), `findRetentionDivergence`(used), `mcnemarExact`(used), `orderCaseFacts`(used), `runPairedAblation`(used), `valid