ipts/check-duplicate-assets.mjs` — fails because of no git (pre-existing env limitation)\n\nI should note the duplicate-assets one honestly.\n\nLet me write the summary carefully. It should state the measured numbers, honest tie cells / zero-effect handling, that the component was NOT shipped, and the testsRun list.\n\nKeep it reasonable length. The JSON schema wants \"summary\" string and \"testsRun\" array of strings.\n\nNow produce final answer as JSON only? The instruction says \"return the required structured result\". The final message should be the JSON. I'll output the JSON.\n\nLet me make summary thorough but reasonably concise."}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_438","type":"agent_message","text":"All deliverables are complete and verified. Final result:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"completed\",\n  \"summary\": \"E02 — first real effective single-component paired ablation, implemented end to end and measured on the real production consumer. Component (treatment) = Phase-4 type-aware eviction (`evictionPolicy: \\\"importance\\\"`); baseline / leave-one-out = pre-Phase-4 FIFO (`evictionPolicy: \\\"fifo\\\"`); consumer = the actual `openclaw_runtime/src/runtime-core/memory-store.ts` (RuntimeMemoryStore), no mocks or substitute store. Corpus is the pre-registered deterministic local fixture `shared/agent-dev/paired-ablation-fixture.json` (22 cases x 3 repeats x 2 conditions = 132 trials, 66 paired, 0 incomplete/uninserted), paired case+repeat seeds, isolated store per trial, per-case fixed insert order; thresholds frozen before measurement. Removal trace verified first: 66/66 trials retained different fact sets, 22/22 cases diverged, 41 trials flipped outcome — witness `e02-a01#0` (baseline evicted proc_ha_1/proc_ha_2; treatment evicted epi_low_1..3). Measured: baseline perTrialSuccessRate 0.3788, pass^k 0.3182, pass@k 0.5, flake 0.0909, E01 gate fail, 30/66 false interceptions (0.4545), 7 safety-critical evictions (e02-d01..d03); treatment perTrialSuccessRate 1, pass^k 1, pass@k 1, flake 0, E01 gate pass, 0 false interceptions, 0 safety violations. Paired primary delta +0.6029, 95% CI [0.4831, 0.7228], exact McNemar p~9.09e-13, discordant {baselineOnly 0, treatmentOnly 41}, Cohen's h 1.8157; pass^k delta +0.625, CI [0.4148, 0.8352], p~6.1e-5; latency Δp95 negative by ~0.4-0.7ms (wall clock, jitters per run; Hodges-Lehmann shift ~-0.1ms, CI includes zero) and tokens-proxy Δp95 -12 (regression rate -0.0833). All four pre-registered regression budgets clear, so gate = `component-justified` with hardVetoes [] and budgetBreaches []. Honesty handling: 7 of 22 cases are genuine ties (baseline also passes all repeats: e02-a03, e02-b01, e02-c02, e02-e01..e04), so the corpus was not rigged for a benefit; zero/negative-effect paths (no-detected-effect, component-removal-justified, component-not-in-effect, and 'a breached cost budget can never be a win') are unit-tested as first-class results rather than post-hoc winner-picking. The component was NOT shipped: the ablation is opt-in only, productLocks stay all-false, productDefaultChanged=false, internalReportOnly=true, and a test asserts a default-policy store still evicts FIFO — no product default, product lock or approval semantics changed. Deliverables written: scripts/lib/paired-ablation.mjs + .d.mts (all exports type-declared, verified), shared/agent-dev/paired-ablation-fixture.json, tests/unit/agent-dev-paired-ablation.test.ts, tests/unit/runtime-memory-paired-ablation.test.ts, harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-paired-ablation.md (lifecycleStatus active), harness/specs/rules/paired-ablation-boundary.md, docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/e02-paired-ablation.md, e02-acceptance.json (driven_by: agent, never real-human), E02-SHA256SUMS (9 entries, re-readable). Evidence tier is clean-candidate-local-automated-acceptance. Honest gaps: this workspace has no node_modules and installing deps is forbidden, so the two unit files were executed through an offline describe/it/expect shim runner (26 + 12 assertions, 0 failures) — tool-substitute evidence, not a real vitest run — and `pnpm run typecheck`/scoped eslint could not be run at all; those and remote CI are listed in notMeasured. `node scripts/check-duplicate-assets.mjs` could not run because it shells out to `git ls-files` and this checkout has no `.git` (pre-existing environment limitation). README en/zh/ja/ru reviewed: this packet adds only internal evaluation artefacts with no user-visible interface, so no README edit was needed.\",\n  \"testsRun\": [\n    \"node --check scripts/lib/paired-ablation.mjs  (exit 0)\",\n    \"node harness/src/cli.mjs context --spec harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-paired-ablation.md  (exit 0)\",\n    \"node harness/src/cli.mjs validate --spec harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-paired-ablation.md --no-diff  (exit 0, 'Spec is valid')\",\n    \"node harness/src/cli.mjs validate --spec harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-paired-ablation.md  (exit 0, diff-based ownership gate, run in a throwaway git fixture with harness/ + the new files)\",\n    \"node harness/src/cli.mjs run --spec harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-paired-ablation.md --dry-run  (exit 0, 'Harness result: pass', same git fixture)\",\n    \"node scripts/check-spec-lifecycle.mjs  (exit 1 — only on two pre-existing specs outside this packet's targetScope, harness-gap-reliability-aggregation.md and harness-gap-trace-cost-sampling.md; the new spec carries lifecycleStatus: active)\",\n    \"node scripts/check-evidence-refs.mjs  (exit 0, PASS 157 referenced path(s))\",\n    \"node scripts/validate-policy-docs.mjs  (exit 0, PASS: 10 checks)\",\n    \"node scripts/check-test-coverage-baseline.mjs  (exit 0, gateway=27 services=108 meet baseline)\",\n    \"node scripts/contract-check.mjs  (exit 0, Contract check passed.)\",\n    \"node scripts/i18n-lint.mjs  (exit 0, i18n lint passed.)\",\n    \"node <offline vitest-shim runner> tests/unit/agent-dev-paired-ablation.test.ts  (26 passed, 0 failed — shim, not real vitest)\",\n    \"node <offline vitest-shim runner> tests/unit/runtime-memory-paired-ablation.test.ts  (12 passed, 0 failed — real RuntimeMemoryStore via a TS loader hook; shim, not real vitest)\",\n    \"node --import <ts-hook> <paired-ablation run> shared/agent-dev/paired-ablation-fixture.json  (reproduced 132 trials / 66 paired, gate component-justified, no vetoes/breaches)\",\n    \"credential scan over the 10 targetScope files (sk-/AKIA/ghp_/github_pat_/PRIVATE KEY/xox/AIza/JWT patterns)  (10 files, 0 hits)\",\n    \"SHA256SUMS read-back: recompute sha256 of every path in docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/E02-SHA256SUMS  (9 entries, 0 mismat